               Sergei Vassilvitskii},
  title     = {Bounding User Contributions: A Bias-Variance Trade-off in Differential Privacy},
  booktitle = {Proceedings of the 36th International Conference on Machine Learning},
  series    = {Proceedings of Machine Learning Research},
  volume    = {97},
  pages     = {263--271},
  publisher = {PMLR},
  year      = {2019},
  annote    = {Metadata VERIFIED against PMLR's BibTeX (author spellings corrected). The CLAIM is
               taken on trust from the prior-art search, not personally verified: that they prove
               the optimal cap is a quantile of the per-user contribution distribution, state it
               must be computed privately, and leave instantiation open. Their x_i is records per
